dropped the body
--
N5008 [class.base.init]/9.2: in a union's constructor, a variant member that
is not designated by a mem-initializer-id is not initialized at all
("otherwise, if the entity is an anonymous union or a variant member,
no initialization is performed"); only `byte' is initialized here.  The
front end nevertheless default-constructs the other variant member `val',
fails because item has no default constructor ("found no match for symbol
'item'") and drops the union constructor, so the byte reads nondet.  This
is libstdc++'s vector::_Temporary_value::_Storage (stl_vector.h:1852, 8
cbmc-cpp descs in the round-163 audit, e.g. vector::insert of a
non-trivial element) and optional::_Storage (optional:209, when the value
type has no default constructor).  Header-free reduction; the libstdc++
shape is `std::vector<item> v; v.reserve(4); v.insert(v.begin(), item(2))'.
Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51 shows the same drop).
